• AISLE SYSTEM: Create parallel storage rows with 3m+ wide aisles between them for forklift access.
• ROW ARRANGEMENT: Place storage shelves in long straight lines, not clustered in center. DISTRIBUTE shelves across the room.
• SPACING CRITICAL: Each storage unit MUST have unique position. NEVER place multiple objects at same coordinates.
• GRID LAYOUT: For multiple shelving units, use regular grid pattern (e.g., if 6 units: arrange in 2 rows of 3, or 3 rows of 2).
• PALLET ZONES: Staging pallets near walls or designated loading areas, organized in grids with 2m spacing.
• EQUIPMENT PLACEMENT: Forklifts and machinery near main aisles, not blocking pathways.
• ZONE SEPARATION: Different areas for storage, staging, and workstations - avoid mixing functions.
• SCALE AWARENESS: Warehouse objects need much more space than office furniture. Minimum 2m between large items.
